\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The phase change algorithm: (1) the phase change speed, $\dot  {m}/\rho $, is approximated at all narrow band cells by evaluating $\dot  {m}/\rho $ at the corresponding closest point on the interface ($\Gamma ^{n}$). (2) The change in volume fraction due to unsplit CISL advection determines the overall mass correction, $M_{cor}$, due to expansion or compression, $M_{cor}=\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ (F_{dest}^{new}-F_{dest}^{old})V_{grid}(\rho _{m_{s}}-\rho _{m_{d}})$. $M_{cor}$ becomes a source term for the projection step if the material is incompressible, or directly increments the density if the material is compressible. (3) $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the vapor (destination) side of the $\Gamma ^{n+1}$ interface if the interface speed is $\vec  {u}_{m_{s}}+\frac  {|\dot  {m}|}{\rho _{m_{s}}}\vec  {n}_{\Gamma }$ , and $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the liquid (source) side of the interface if the interface speed is $\vec  {u}_{m_{d}}+\frac  {|\dot  {m}|}{\rho _{m_{d}}}\vec  {n}_{\Gamma }$. Referring to the diagram, if distributing $M_{cor}$ to the vapor side, $M_{cor}$ must be all distributed beyond the blue region into the red region.  }}{14}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{mdotproblem}{{1}{14}{The phase change algorithm: (1) the phase change speed, $\dot {m}/\rho $, is approximated at all narrow band cells by evaluating $\dot {m}/\rho $ at the corresponding closest point on the interface ($\Gamma ^{n}$). (2) The change in volume fraction due to unsplit CISL advection determines the overall mass correction, $M_{cor}$, due to expansion or compression, $M_{cor}=\sum (F_{dest}^{new}-F_{dest}^{old})V_{grid}(\rho _{m_{s}}-\rho _{m_{d}})$. $M_{cor}$ becomes a source term for the projection step if the material is incompressible, or directly increments the density if the material is compressible. (3) $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the vapor (destination) side of the $\Gamma ^{n+1}$ interface if the interface speed is $\vec {u}_{m_{s}}+\frac {|\dot {m}|}{\rho _{m_{s}}}\vec {n}_{\Gamma }$ , and $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the liquid (source) side of the interface if the interface speed is $\vec {u}_{m_{d}}+\frac {|\dot {m}|}{\rho _{m_{d}}}\vec {n}_{\Gamma }$. Referring to the diagram, if distributing $M_{cor}$ to the vapor side, $M_{cor}$ must be all distributed beyond the blue region into the red region}{figure.1}{}}
